# Enhanced GCP Security Agent - Cursor Rules
# ALWAYS USE VERTEX AI AND CLOUD RUN FOR ALL OPERATIONS

## Google Cloud Platform Architecture Requirements

### Vertex AI Integration
- **ALWAYS use Vertex AI for all LLM operations** - Never use Google AI API directly
- Use Application Default Credentials (ADC) for authentication to Vertex AI
- Set GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT and GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION environment variables
- Use `gemini-2.0-flash-exp` model through Vertex AI endpoints
- All ADK agents MUST be configured to use Vertex AI backend
- Never pass api_key parameter to Agent constructor - use ADC only

### Cloud Run Deployment Strategy
- **Target Cloud Run for all deployment scenarios**
- Configure containerized applications with proper health checks
- Use Cloud Run service-to-service authentication
- Implement proper resource limits and scaling policies
- Configure VPC connector for secure communication
- Use Cloud Run jobs for batch processing tasks

### Authentication and Authorization
- **MANDATORY: Use Application Default Credentials (ADC) everywhere**
- Configure service accounts with least privilege access
- Use Cloud IAM roles for fine-grained permissions
- Implement proper OIDC token validation for service-to-service calls
- Never hardcode API keys or credentials in code

## Core Development Principles

### Code Organization
- Encapsulate all code within separate functions to improve organization and maintainability
- Use descriptive function names that clearly indicate their purpose
- Organize related functions into logical modules and services
- Separate concerns: UI, business logic, API calls, and data processing should be in different functions

### Streamlit-Specific Rules
- Expanders may not be nested inside other expanders
- Columns can only be placed inside other columns up to one level of nesting
- Never use st.experimental_* functions - refer to current Streamlit documentation
- Always include submit buttons in forms using st.form_submit_button()
- Do not run 'streamlit run' commands as the app will already be running via run.sh
- Use st.session_state for maintaining state across interactions

### Dependency Management
- Update requirements.txt as needed with no version numbers
- Always verify that new dependencies are added to both main requirements.txt and backend/requirements.txt as appropriate
- Ensure streamlit-agraph is included for DAG visualization
- Include all OpenTelemetry dependencies for tracing support

## Security Agent Specific Requirements

### Tracing and Monitoring
- Always use OpenTelemetry spans for agent operations in the backend
- Include meaningful span attributes (user_id, operation_name, duration, etc.)
- Implement proper error handling and status codes in traces
- Use the TracingService for managing trace data and analytics
- Ensure all agent queries are traced through the agent_service.py

### OIDC Authentication Flow
- Maintain the demonstration nature of OIDC flows - no real credentials required
- Use proper Mermaid diagram syntax for authentication flow visualization
- Include all three OIDC flows: Authorization Code, Client Credentials, Token Exchange
- Ensure OIDC state management is handled properly in session state

### Agent DAG Visualization
- Use streamlit-agraph for interactive DAG visualization
- Include timing information in node labels (e.g., "operation_name\n(123ms)")
- Provide clickable nodes with detailed span information
- Show both agent execution traces and OIDC flow diagrams
- Include performance metrics and timeline charts using Plotly

### MSA Analysis Features
- Maintain the parsing capabilities for Microsoft Service Agreements
- Support multiple input methods: text input, file upload, sample data
- Include Google Cloud organization scanning simulation
- Show impact analysis with risk levels and project information
- Provide comprehensive results visualization

### Security Evaluation
- Support all evaluation types: Security, Compliance, Threat Intelligence, Configuration
- Include multiple compliance frameworks (SOC2, ISO27001, GDPR, HIPAA, PCI_DSS)
- Display results in organized tabs with appropriate visualizations
- Provide comprehensive metrics and scoring

### Backend API Integration
- Always use the make_backend_request() function for API calls
- Include proper error handling for all backend requests
- Use appropriate HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
- Handle timeout scenarios gracefully
- Display meaningful error messages to users

### Google Cloud Services Integration
- **Use Vertex AI for all LLM/Agent operations** - set model='gemini-2.0-flash-exp'
- Use Cloud Run for hosting both frontend (Streamlit) and backend (FastAPI)
- Use Cloud Storage for file uploads and data persistence
- Use Cloud Trace for OpenTelemetry distributed tracing
- Use Cloud Logging for application logs and monitoring
- Use Cloud IAM for service authentication and authorization
- Use Cloud Secret Manager for sensitive configuration data

### Container and Deployment Configuration
- Create Dockerfile for both frontend and backend services
- Use multi-stage builds for optimized container images
- Configure Cloud Run services with proper CPU/memory limits
- Set up proper environment variable management
- Implement graceful shutdown handling
- Configure liveness and readiness probes

## Code Quality Standards

### Error Handling
- Always include try-catch blocks for external API calls
- Provide user-friendly error messages in the UI
- Log errors appropriately for debugging
- Handle network timeouts and connection failures gracefully

### Performance
- Use background tasks for long-running operations
- Implement proper loading indicators (st.spinner)
- Cache expensive operations when appropriate
- Optimize database queries and API calls

### Documentation
- Include comprehensive docstrings for all functions
- Document complex algorithms and business logic
- Provide clear comments for non-obvious code sections
- Maintain up-to-date README and API documentation

## UI/UX Requirements

### Navigation
- Use consistent sidebar navigation with emoji icons
- Implement clear page routing and state management
- Provide breadcrumbs or clear indication of current location
- Include "Back" or "Reset" options where appropriate

### Data Visualization
- Use Plotly for interactive charts and graphs
- Include appropriate chart types for different data (bar, line, timeline)
- Provide clear legends and axis labels
- Use consistent color schemes throughout the application

### Forms and Inputs
- Always include submit buttons in forms
- Provide clear validation messages
- Use appropriate input types (text, textarea, selectbox, multiselect)
- Include helpful placeholder text and descriptions

### Responsive Design
- Use Streamlit columns for responsive layouts
- Ensure content is readable on different screen sizes
- Provide appropriate spacing and padding
- Use consistent styling throughout the application

## Development Workflow

### Code Review
- Always look through more code in the codebase when generating answers
- Grep the whole codebase for methods to trace function calls end-to-end
- A more accurate response is better than a quick one
- Ensure no existing functionality is removed unless explicitly requested

### Testing
- Verify all new features work with the run.sh script
- Test both frontend and backend functionality
- Ensure all dependencies are properly installed
- Validate that tracing and visualization features work correctly

### Deployment
- Use the run.sh script for one-command deployment
- Ensure all environment variables are properly set
- Verify that both services start correctly
- Check that all API endpoints are accessible

## Specific Feature Requirements

### Run.sh Script
- Must install all required dependencies including streamlit-agraph and OpenTelemetry
- Should verify critical dependencies after installation
- Must set up proper tracing environment variables
- Should provide comprehensive startup information
- Must handle both local and Google Cloud configurations

### Agent Service
- Implement OpenTelemetry tracing for all operations
- Use proper span naming and attributes
- Handle session management correctly
- Provide detailed agent information and tool lists

### Frontend Application
- Include all visualization tabs: Agent Traces, OIDC Flows, Performance
- Implement interactive DAG visualization with streamlit-agraph
- Provide comprehensive security evaluation UI
- Support MSA analysis with multiple input methods
- Include incident response management interface

### Backend Services
- Implement all API endpoints with proper error handling
- Include tracing service for managing trace data
- Support all security evaluation types
- Provide comprehensive compliance checking
- Include MSA parsing and analysis capabilities

## Future Improvements

After implementing any feature, consider these potential improvements:
- Enhanced error handling and user feedback
- Additional visualization options and chart types
- More comprehensive security evaluation criteria
- Extended compliance framework support
- Advanced tracing and monitoring capabilities
- Better performance optimization
- Enhanced user experience and accessibility
- Additional authentication methods and security features

## Common Issues to Address

- Missing submit buttons in forms
- Nested expanders or columns beyond allowed limits
- Deprecated Streamlit functions (st.experimental_*)
- Missing or incorrect dependencies in requirements.txt
- Improper error handling in API calls
- Inconsistent state management
- Poor performance with large datasets
- Accessibility issues in the UI
- Missing documentation or unclear code comments

Remember: The goal is to create a maintainable, well-documented, and user-friendly security evaluation platform that can be easily understood and extended by both humans and LLMs. 